          "entities": {},
          "text": "José Antonio Kast was elected president of Chile in the runoff election, defeating his communist opponent .\n\nHis father, Michael Kast (full name Michael Martín Kast Schindele), was born on April 2, 1924, in the Bavarian village of Thalkirchdorf in Germany; he voluntarily joined Adolf Hitler's Nazi Party in September 1942 at age 18 (membership number 9271831), initially served on garrison duty in France in 1942, then fought on the Eastern Front against the Soviet Union from 1943 to 1944, including specifically in the Battle of Korsun–Cherkassy (also known as the Korsun Pocket).\n\nHe rose to the rank of Oberleutnant (first lieutenant) in the Wehrmacht infantry, was later transferred to Italy in 1944–1945 where he defended the Gothic Line in the Apennine Mountains, was captured by American forces near Trento in May 1945, and emigrated to Chile in 1950! 🫠"
        },
